    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To create the file dead_letter.py that sends failed messages to a dead-letter destination using a concrete external provider, I will choose AWS SNS (Simple Notification Service) as the provider. This choice is based on its robust messaging capabilities and the ability to handle dead-letter queues. The code will import the boto3 library, which is the AWS SDK for Python, to interact with AWS services. The boto3 library will be used to publish messages to an SNS topic and handle failures by sending messages to a dead-letter queue. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789890067008,
          "start": 1789890063499
